# Direct dependencies. Edit this file, then regenerate the pinned
# requirements.txt next to it:
#
#   uv pip compile google_scholar_crawler/requirements.in \
#       --python-platform linux --python-version 3.12 \
#       -o google_scholar_crawler/requirements.txt
#
# scholarly declares all twelve of its own dependencies without upper bounds,
# so leaving the transitive set unpinned means any upstream major release can
# break this crawler with nothing here changing. It happened twice in a week:
# free-proxy changed get_proxy_list()'s signature, then bibtexparser 2.0 dropped
# the module scholarly imports at load time.
